Our Lord!"")";Sahih al-Bukhari 6523, Book 81, Hadith 112;;question #2;How does the hadith illustrate the concept of divine justice for disbelievers in the hereafter?
"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""You will meet Allah barefooted, naked, walking on feet, and uncircumcised.""";Sahih al-Bukhari 6524, Book 81, Hadith 113;;question #2;How does the description of the Day of Judgment emphasize human vulnerability and equality before Allah?
"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) while he was delivering a sermon on a pulpit, saying, ""You will meet Allah 
barefooted, naked, and uncircumcised.""";Sahih al-Bukhari 6525, Book 81, Hadith 114;;question #2;How does the hadith describe the physical condition of people during the resurrection?
"The Prophet (ﷺ) stood up among us and addressed (saying) ""You will be gathered, barefooted, naked, and 
